<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE" ;
  triage:title "Multiple graft receiver sessions for the same (workspace root, team, agent) are unsafe: last bind wins, either close deletes the shared endpoint record" ;
  triage:description "The graft receiver endpoint record at .atm/graft/<team>/<agent>.json is keyed only by (workspace root, team, agent) via graft_receiver_record_path_from_root/graft_receiver_record_path_from_home (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs). GraftReceiverListener::bind (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:165-197) has no exclusivity check against an already-active receiver for that path: it calls prepare_receiver_record_parent, which unconditionally removes any pre-existing record file (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:359-377: 'if record_path.exists() { fs::remove_file(record_path)? }'), then binds a fresh TcpListener on an ephemeral loopback port and writes a brand-new record via write_receiver_record using OpenOptions::write(true).create(true).truncate(true) (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:393-413) — a plain truncating write with no lock/PID check/staleness check. Two separate processes (e.g. two Hermes gateway instances, or a stale process plus a fresh restart) can each independently call bind() for the same (team, agent): both successfully bind their own TCP listener, but only the record from whichever bind() ran last is on disk, so senders (deliver_graft_post_send, crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:306-343) only ever reach the most-recently-activated receiver. The other live receiver is bound and listening but permanently unreachable from any sender. Additionally, GraftReceiverListener's Drop impl (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:287-293: 'let _ = fs::remove_file(&self.record_path);') deletes the record file unconditionally on close/drop, with no check for whether the file it is deleting still corresponds to its own listener. So if the OLDER of two concurrently-bound receivers is closed after the newer one has overwritten the record, the close deletes the NEWER (currently-active, currently-referenced) receiver's record, silently disconnecting the still-live receiver from all future senders even though that receiver process itself keeps running." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "architecture_review" ;
  triage:category "HERMES-GRAFT-ARCHITECTURE" ;
  triage:severity "major" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "component" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:blockingCurrentMerge false ;
  triage:note "Architecture gap, not a regression in the reviewed merge (integrate/phase-ai-31-33@21957012) — single-active-receiver-per-(workspace,team,agent) has always been the implicit contract and nothing in this merge changed it. Do not fix under time pressure or as an incidental change. A safe multi-receiver-or-enforced-singleton design (e.g. PID/lock-file exclusivity on bind, or record generation/ownership token checked before Drop deletes it) requires an approved design before implementation; scope belongs to a future planning sprint, not the current phase-ai-31-33 branch. Until an approved replacement design lands, the current one-active-receiver-per-endpoint invariant must be preserved and operationally enforced (never run two receiver processes for the same workspace/team/agent concurrently) rather than patched ad hoc." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:ARCH-CTM-REVIEW-phase-ai-31-33 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE/bind-overwrite> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE/record-truncate-write> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE/drop-unconditional-delete> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/phase-AI/integrate-phase-ai-31-33> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/phase-AI/future-planning-sprint> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "integrate/phase-ai-31-33" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-GRAFT-RECEIVER-SINGLETON-UNSAFE/bind-overwrite>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs" ;
  triage:line 359 ;
  triage:snippet "fn prepare_receiver_record_parent(record_path: &Path) -> Result<(), AtmError> { ... if record_path.exists() { fs::remove_file(record_path)... } } — bind() unconditionally clears any pre-existing endpoint record with no ownership/liveness check before a new receiver claims the path." ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
